  "overview": {
    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Malia M. Cohen, a Democrat, is the California State Controller. She was elected in 2022. She is seeking re-election in 2026. She previously served on the California State Board of Equalization, chairing it in 2019 and 2022, and was president of the San Francisco Board of Supervisors, where she chaired the Budget and Finance Committee. As president of the San Francisco Employees’ Retirement System, she led efforts to divest from fossil fuels and moved $100 million into a fossil fuel-free index fund.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Malia M. Cohen, a Democrat, is the California State Controller.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          { "text": "She was elected in 2022.", "cites": [2] },
          { "text": "She is seeking re-election in 2026.", "cites": [1] },
          {
            "text": "She previously served on the California State Board of Equalization, chairing it in 2019 and 2022, and was president of the San Francisco Board of Supervisors, where she chaired the Budget and Finance Committee.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "As president of the San Francisco Employees’ Retirement System, she led efforts to divest from fossil fuels and moved $100 million into a fossil fuel-free index fund.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Her campaign says she has expanded public access to financial and payroll data, released monthly cash reports, and advanced efforts to modernize the state payroll system. In 2025, she cautioned that the state faces significant structural deficits and urged fiscal prudence. In October 2026, after reporting that state spending was running above budget projections, she called for discipline to protect reserves and ensure the state can meet its obligations. She also chairs the Franchise Tax Board and sits on the boards of CalPERS and CalSTRS.",
        "cites": [1, 4, 5, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Her campaign says she has expanded public access to financial and payroll data, released monthly cash reports, and advanced efforts to modernize the state payroll system.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2025, she cautioned that the state faces significant structural deficits and urged fiscal prudence.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "In October 2026, after reporting that state spending was running above budget projections, she called for discipline to protect reserves and ensure the state can meet its obligations.",
            "cites": [5]
          },
          {
            "text": "She also chairs the Franchise Tax Board and sits on the boards of CalPERS and CalSTRS.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A state audit found the controller’s office mishandled more than $33,000 in employee overpayments and did not detect managers working remotely from out of state.",
        "cites": [6],
